export anchor BrightConfidentStyle:
    number: 220
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Bright confident
    idea: A crisp white workspace under a bold saturated blue band, with big friendly figures, rounded cards that lift off the band and one confident blue doing all the work.
    base: light
    palette:
        blue: #1650f0, the band, primary buttons, this week bars, rings, links and focus
        blueDeep: #0b2f9e, blue text on white and tint and the current nav label
        blueTint: #e9efff, icon bubbles, department tags, ring tracks and last week fill
        blueLine: #b9cbff, field and secondary button borders, never text
        white: #ffffff, cards, panels and text on the band
        page: #f6f8fc, the page below the band
        ink: #111a2e, text and figures
        ink2: #435069, secondary text and labels
        line: #e1e6f0, card borders and dividers
        green: #137a3a, On track with a solid circle and check
        amber: #975a00, At risk with a solid triangle and bang
        red: #c4242b, Behind with a solid square and down arrow, and overdue
        redTint: #fdecec, the overdue bubble and the Review now pill
    type:
        One stack, Inter, Segoe UI Variable Display, Segoe UI, system-ui,
        Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial. The greeting is 40px 800 at minus
        0.03em, KPI figures 36px 800, section titles 22px 800, card titles
        18px 700, body 15px, meta and labels 14px 600.
    layout:
        A full width saturated blue band opens the page. Its top row holds
        a white rounded square mark with a blue check and the brand in
        white, the six nav items as pills inside a translucent pill track
        with the current one white and blue, then a white pill search, a
        round translucent bell and a white initials disc. Under it the
        hero shows Good to see you, Mara in big white type, the date with
        a line saying 73 tasks closed this week and 14 more than last,
        and a white pill reading 4 tasks are overdue with a clock and a
        Review now chip. A large white New project button sits at the
        hero's right. Four white KPI cards with 20px corners and soft
        shadows overlap the bottom of the band, each a tinted icon bubble
        beside a big figure and its label, the overdue one red. Below, Your
        projects is a three by two grid of white cards, each with a
        department tag, the name, tasks done and percent, a ring with the
        percent at right and a footer with a solid status chip and the due
        date with days left. Last comes a two to one row, a chart card with
        three totals for this week, last week and the change over grouped
        bars by weekday, last week outlined in blue on tint and this week
        solid blue with values on top, and a team activity card with
        initials discs. Below 980px nav scrolls on its own row, KPIs and
        cards go two across, and on phones everything stacks in one column
        with the chart scrolling sideways.
    spacing: An 8px unit, generous. 20px gaps between cards, 24px card padding, 40px between sections.
    density: Low to medium. Six project cards, big figures and plenty of air.
    corners: Round. 20px cards, 12px buttons and fields, and pills for nav, tags, search and the overdue alert.
    borders: 1px line on cards. 2px blueLine on fields and secondary buttons.
    shadows: KPI cards float with a 12px offset 32px blur shadow at 10 percent ink so they lift off the band. The hero button has a deeper blue shadow.
    icons:
        Line icons at 2px stroke sized to their text. Status icons are 16px
        solid shapes, a circle with a check, a triangle with a bang and a
        square with a down arrow, beside their word.
    focus: A 3px solid blue outline offset 3px, and white on the blue band.
    tone: Upbeat and direct, such as Good to see you, Mara, Review now and Up 24 percent.
